From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom: expose MSM8226 short-descriptor block sizes

Expose the 64KB large-page and 1MB section sizes already implemented
by ARM_V7S and used by the exact MSM8226 BSP. Keep other contexts
restricted to their existing 4KB pages.

This enables a controlled section-mapping diagnostic through the normal
IOMMU API. Hardware ATOS has repeatedly timed out at page level2 with
valid CPU-visible L1/L2 tables; a section mapping can test the level1
walk without editing live page tables or replacing the scanout buffer.
No framebuffer address, GPU configuration or PLL setting is changed.

Link: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226/blob/3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256/drivers/iommu/msm_iommu_pagetable.c

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index b0feed7f0..37a319bef 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -461,6 +461,7 @@ static int qcom_iommu_init_domain(struct iommu_domain *domain,
 static struct iommu_domain *qcom_iommu_domain_alloc_paging(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct qcom_iommu_domain *qcom_domain;
+	struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu = dev_iommu_priv_get(dev);
 
 	/*
 	 * Allocate the domain and initialise some of its data structures.
@@ -474,6 +475,9 @@ static struct iommu_domain *qcom_iommu_domain_alloc_paging(struct device *dev)
 	mutex_init(&qcom_domain->init_mutex);
 	spin_lock_init(&qcom_domain->pgtbl_lock);
 	qcom_domain->domain.pgsize_bitmap = SZ_4K;
+	/* MSM8226 BSP supports short-descriptor large pages and sections. */
+	if (qcom_iommu && qcom_iommu->short_desc)
+		qcom_domain->domain.pgsize_bitmap |= SZ_64K | SZ_1M;
 
 	return &qcom_domain->domain;
 }
